  m_Name: unit_860828
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  unitName: Dusk Haunter Kirke
  unitId: 860828
  unitNumber: 8626
  description: "Stick around the alleys at midnight long enough, and you're bound
    to run into a masked young man perched atop a wire fence. Without another word,
    he'll follow you around from a distance, but he never seems to be in the vicinity
    when you look. Kirke has become something of an urban legend in the city, but
    as long as the celestial dog was able to satisfy his protective streak, he was
    more than happy to be a ghost.One of the contenders in Emperor Yu's competition
    in search for the perfect assistant (a role many believed he was already qualified
    for), Kirke did as his nature commanded: become a worthy companion and protector
    of humans, as he did in the days before his ascension. But the new world had
    shed its old ways, and it was getting increasingly difficult to convince any
    human of his good intentions in the traditional fashion.Not to be dissuaded,
    Kirke donned a new coat and collar and called upon the zeitgeist\u2014brooding,
    dark, and melancholy creatures skulking away from the light. He blended in seamlessly
    with the local youth, even sparking interest among patrons of a nearby underground
    club. Kirke would soon learn that the celestial Dragon\u2014now named Noxa\u2014was
    their local celebrity. She was amused to see him stalk into her den with several
    of her regulars, but nevertheless welcomed him to the sleepless city.Having found
    a place in his new pack, Kirke delights in safeguarding his young charges. His
    youthful appearance belied centuries of guardianship, and many a bully or thug
    has broken speed records escaping from his shadowy hounds.After all, Kirke was
    not one for words; his bite was far, far worse than his bark."
  summonDesc: Huh. You found me after all.<br>Go on. I'll follow.<br>Don't pay too
    much attention to me.
  fusionDesc: You again...<br>I'm pretty sure I told you not to come find me.<br>...But
    thanks.
  evoDesc: Hear that? The howling?<br>Did you think it was all just a myth?
  element: 6
  rarity: 7
